 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "ketubot.72a.5",
   "daf": "72a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "אוֹ שֶׁתְּהֵא מְמַלְּאָה וּמְעָרָה לְאַשְׁפָּה. וְתִיעְבֵּיד! אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: שֶׁתְּמַלֵּא וְנוֹפֶצֶת. בְּמַתְנִיתָא תַּנָּא: שֶׁתְּמַלֵּא עֲשָׂרָה כַּדֵּי מַיִם וּתְעָרֶה לְאַשְׁפָּה.",
   "en": "The mishna stated: «Or» he said the vow will be void on condition «that she fill» something up «and pour» it «into the refuse.» The Gemara asks: «And let her do it. Rav Yehuda said» that «Shmuel said:» The mishna’s intention is «that» he demanded that «she fill» herself up «and» then «shake» herself out. This is a euphemistic way of saying that the husband wants her to take measures to prevent herself from becoming pregnant, and she is permitted to protest this. «It was taught in a baraita:» The case is «that» he told her «to fill» up «ten jugs of water and pour» them «into the refuse,» a task that involves pointless effort and appears foolish."
  }
 ],
